What are the perils/liabilities for which cover is provided in each of the three Sections?
1. Loss of or Damage to the Vehicle Insured
provides protection for any damages to your vehicle arising out of / caused due to:
1. fire explosion self-ignition or lightning;
2. burglary housebreaking or theft;
3. riot and strike;
4. earthquake (fire and shock damage);
5. flood typhoon hurricane storm tempest inundation cyclone hailstorm frost;
6. accidental external means;
7. malicious act;
8. terrorist activity;
9. whilst in transit by road rail inland-waterway lift elevator or air;
10. landslide rockslide.
Subject to a deduction for depreciation at the rates mentioned below in respect of parts replaced:
1. For all rubber/nylon/plastic parts, tyres and tubes, batteries and air bags - 50%
2. For fibre glass components - 30%
3. For all parts made of glass - Nil
4. Rate of Depreciation for Painting - In the case of painting, the depreciation rate of 50% shall be
applied only on the material cost of total painting charges. In case of a consolidated bill for painting
charges, the material component shall be considered as 25% of the total painting charges for the
purpose of applying the depreciation.
